 "notes": "June 1990 zoning sheet 10. A single heavy frame rule on all four sides; the legend strip (district key, code note, north arrow, scale bar, sheet number) and the title strip are ruled off below the map by a thick bar, so the bottom side sits ~2 px above it (rule 3; full width, no notch). Left, top and right ~2 px inside the frame rule's inner edge (left x ~78-91 drifting right top to bottom, right ~3216-3227, top y ~548-559, legend bar ~4111 left to ~4102 right). The rule's inner corners have small fillets (top-left ~10 px, top-right ~4 px, and a step at the bottom-right): the outline cuts each with 2-3 extra points so the fillet ink stays outside (README rule 2 is about decorative arcs; these are just the rule's rounded corners). No notches, no remove polygon. The dashed line ~100 px above the legend bar and CANDLESTICK PARK, BAY VIEW PARK lettering are map. No ink under the outline.",
 "drawn_by": "Claude (TC, test set), 2026-11-21: rule edges measured column by column from page.png (thickest/nearest dark run per column), smoothed with a robust local line (+-120 px), outline set 2 px inside the edge, points every ~150-250 px; every vertex checked on full-resolution crops; drawn from the scan and README only (no model output)"
